# Integration Steps — Do These in Order

## STEP 1: Add dependencies to pom.xml
Open pom.xml and add inside <dependencies>:

  <!-- Swagger -->
  <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
      <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
      <version>2.3.0</version>
  </dependency>

  <!-- Validation -->
  <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
  </dependency>

---

## STEP 2: Create dto/ folder in Spring Boot
Path: src/main/java/com/example/demo/dto/

Copy these files there:
  - RegisterRequest.java
  - LoginRequest.java

---

## STEP 3: Create exception/ folder in Spring Boot
Path: src/main/java/com/example/demo/exception/

Copy this file there:
  - GlobalExceptionHandler.java

---

## STEP 4: Replace existing files
Replace these files with the new versions:
  - userService.java        → src/main/java/com/example/demo/Service/
  - AuthController.java     → src/main/java/com/example/demo/Controller/
  - JwtFilter.java          → src/main/java/com/example/demo/security/

Add new file:
  - SwaggerConfig.java      → src/main/java/com/example/demo/Config/

---

## STEP 5: Fix existing users in MySQL
Because passwords are now BCrypt hashed, existing plain-text
passwords in the database won't work anymore.

Option A — Delete all users and re-register:
  DELETE FROM user;

Option B — Re-register via the app with a new account.

---

## STEP 6: Restart Spring Boot
  mvn spring-boot:run

---

## STEP 7: Test Swagger
Open in browser:
  http://localhost:8082/swagger-ui/index.html

You should see all your endpoints documented with an Authorize button.

---

## STEP 8: Push README.md to GitHub
Copy README.md to the root of your project and push:
  git add README.md
  git commit -m "Add project README"
  git push